---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`Fourth Down Calculator | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Explore real NFL fourth-down situations with a custom matchup-aware calculator built on nfl4th models." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="project-header">
				<h1>Fourth Down Calculator</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">Explore real NFL fourth-down decisions with matchup-aware win probability estimates.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="iframe-container glass-card">
				<iframe 
					src="https://LukeBDaniel.github.io/fourth-down-calc/" 
					title="Fourth Down Calculator Application"
					frameborder="0"
					allowfullscreen
				></iframe>
			</div>

			<div class="prose glass-card mt-4">
				<h3>About this Project</h3>
				<p>Fourth Down Calculator compares going for it, kicking a field goal, and punting by expected win probability. Users can build a hypothetical situation or select an NFL game and load a real fourth-down play, then compare the model’s recommendation with the team’s actual decision and the play’s outcome.</p>
				<p>I extended the published nfl4th models with a custom adjustment layer that accounts for the matchup: offensive conversion ability, defensive resistance, kicker accuracy by distance, temperature, wind, drive-level performance, and kickoff return and coverage tendencies. A matchup panel shows the context behind the estimates alongside the game’s spread, total, and stadium conditions.</p>
				<p>The React and TypeScript frontend runs calculations in a browser Web Worker. A Python data pipeline processes nflverse play-by-play into team and kicker ratings and a browsable archive of real game situations. The current archive covers games from the 2024–2026 seasons.</p>
				<p>This is an ongoing personal project. I’m continuing to refine the model and its evaluation; historical plays are explored using the current ratings, rather than ratings reconstructed as of each game.</p>
                <div style="margin-top: 1.5em; display: flex; gap: 1em; flex-wrap: wrap;">
                    <a href="https://LukeBDaniel.github.io/fourth-down-calc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn glass-card">Open Full Page</a>
                </div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.project-header {
		margin-bottom: 1.5em;
	}
	.iframe-container {
		width: 100%;
		height: 85vh;
		min-height: 700px;
		padding: 0;
		overflow: hidden;
		margin-bottom: 1.5em;
	}
	iframe {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		border: none;
		background: transparent;
	}
	.subtitle {
		font-size: 1.25em;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
	.mt-4 {
		margin-top: 1.5em;
	}
    .btn {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.5em 1em;
        text-decoration: none;
        color: var(--accent);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        border-radius: 4px;
        transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
    }
    .btn:hover {
        background-color: var(--bg-card);
    }
</style>
